## Objective
1. To understand and implement a Binary Search Tree (BST) in C++.
2. To construct a BST by inserting elements according to BST properties.
3. To find the minimum element by traversing the leftmost nodes.
4. To find the maximum element by traversing the rightmost nodes.
5. To avoid visiting every node while finding the minimum and maximum elements.
6. To analyze the time complexity of minimum and maximum operations in a BST.
